, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 11{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=9$ and ${y}_{2}=-49.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -49\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
